                     <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="org_4">Canterbury, Kent. Benedictine
                           cathedral priory of Holy Trinity or Christ Church</orgName><p><ref
                              target="https://mlgb.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/catalog/book_1250">London,
                              British Library, Cotton MS Otho D. viii, fols. 8–173</ref>, and
                           Cambridge, Trinity College, O. 2. 51, flyleaves, are fragments of one
                           volume. The hand is recognisably that of Christ Church. The flyleaves
                           bear the 13th-century title 'Passionale sancti Ignacii . primum', which
                           corresponds to the wording of an entry in the Eastry catalogue from the
                           cathedral. End part of contents list (= items 18–26 in Otho D.viii) on
                           front flyleaf of Trinity, title on end flyleaf of Trinity. See Ancient
                           Libraries, p. 52, no. 360.</p><note type="MLGB3_medievalCatalogueNotes"
                           >Cat. 360</note></provenance>
                     <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"><persName>Wm. Bowier</persName>. See
                        Cambridge, Corpus Christi College, MS 298, art. 19, extract 'ex quodam
                        vetusto libro quondam ecclesie Cantuar. iam in manibus mri Bower. Liber
                        vocatur passionale S. Ignatii'.</provenance>
